118
00:07:44.113 --> 00:07:45.990
Core Concepts, Beginner to Deep.

119
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:50.184
Intuition: an air-traffic controller for scooters.

120
00:07:50.464 --> 00:07:58.677
A controller has a radar (positions), a map of airspace (zones), a queue of planes wanting to land (orders), and runways (riders).

121
00:07:58.957 --> 00:08:11.139
They don't assign the nearest runway to each plane the moment it appears; they plan a few minutes ahead, pair things efficiently, and tell each plane an honest arrival time, updated as conditions change.

122
00:08:11.419 --> 00:08:15.621
Dispatch works the same way, with the radar fed by 50,000 phones.

123
00:08:16.971 --> 00:08:17.931
Requirements.

124
00:08:18.211 --> 00:08:19.065
Functional.

125
00:08:19.345 --> 00:08:26.555
Decide if an address is serviceable and by which store (polygon zones, with overrides for rain, events and store load).

126
00:08:26.835 --> 00:08:31.657
Track rider positions and states; show the customer the rider on a map with an ETA.

127
00:08:31.937 --> 00:08:36.118
Assign packed orders to riders, with batching; reassign on problems.

128
00:08:36.398 --> 00:08:39.982
Rider app: offers, navigation, proof of delivery, earnings.

129
00:08:40.262 --> 00:08:41.371
Non-functional.

130
00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:46.583
Serviceability lookup 5 ms; nearest riders 10 ms.

131
00:08:46.863 --> 00:08:54.159
Ingest ~12,500 pings per second (peaks ~20k), live positions 5 s old.

132
00:08:54.439 --> 00:08:59.217
Dispatch decisions within seconds of an order being packed (or predicted to be packed).

133
00:08:59.497 --> 00:09:04.788
ETA error small enough that promises hold ≥ 90% of the time.

134
