235
00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.609
Order safety: phones buffer and resend.

236
00:14:33.889 --> 00:14:40.289
Compare timestamps atomically (Lua, or a conditional update), or late pings move riders backwards.

237
00:14:40.569 --> 00:14:44.686
Batching: one round trip per ping caps throughput; batch per consumer poll.

238
00:14:44.966 --> 00:14:48.187
Thinning: the live index needs news, not every ping.

239
00:14:48.467 --> 00:14:51.155
Stationary riders at the store send nothing new.

240
00:14:51.435 --> 00:14:53.185
Raw pings still go to history.

241
00:14:53.465 --> 00:15:01.401
GPS noise: snap to roads, drop impossible jumps (speed 80 km per hour), and smooth positions for display.

242
00:15:02.751 --> 00:15:09.364
Battery and data: adaptive ping rates (faster while delivering, slower while idle) are the biggest lever of all.

243
