00:25:31.218 --> 00:25:33.138
Geo (ADR-330).

385
00:25:33.418 --> 00:25:39.370
Cells, then candidate stores in memory in every checkout pod; overrides applied at request time.

386
00:25:39.650 --> 00:25:42.402
Telemetry (ADR-331).

387
00:25:42.682 --> 00:25:51.578
48 partitions; consumers batch 200 or 50 ms; idle riders ping every 15 s, delivering riders every 4 s.

388
00:25:51.858 --> 00:25:54.354
Dispatch (ADR-332).

389
00:25:54.634 --> 00:26:04.127
Costs = predicted delivery time + promise-breach penalty + batch detour; Hungarian algorithm per cluster; offers expire in 20 s.

390
00:26:04.407 --> 00:26:06.498
ETA (ADR-333).

391
00:26:06.778 --> 00:26:13.199
Daily training on the last 8 weeks; door time per building with shrinkage to the neighbourhood mean for sparse buildings.

392
00:26:14.549 --> 00:26:17.045
Tracking (ADR-334).

393
00:26:17.325 --> 00:26:20.013
Smoothed positions; last updated when stale.

394
00:26:20.293 --> 00:26:21.317
Consequences.

395
00:26:21.597 --> 00:26:26.867
More models to train and monitor; dispatch complexity; building-level data to maintain.

396
00:26:27.147 --> 00:26:34.251
In return: honest promises, faster deliveries at the same fleet size, and a live index that stays fresh at peak.

